      "synthesis": {
        "main_text_has_explicit_synthesis": true,
        "si_used": false,
        "procedure": "Schiff-base ligands H2L-H/NO2/CH3 were prepared by the reported condensation of o-vanillin with 2-aminophenol, 4-nitro-2-aminophenol, or 4-methyl-2-aminophenol in methanol. Complexes 1–3 were obtained under the same mild conditions by reacting Dy(NO3)3·6H2O (0.2 mmol) with the corresponding Schiff-base ligand (0.2 mmol) and Ph3PO (0.4 mmol) in the presence of triethylamine (0.4 mmol). For 1 the ligand is H2L-NO2. Suitable single crystals of 1 were obtained by slow evaporation of the methanolic solution after five days.",
